job.description:
At EY, we’re all in to shape your future with confidence.
We’ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.
Join EY and help to build a better working world.
The opportunity: your next adventure awaits
EY's Transactions Corporate Finance (TCF) department is a unique nexus between the corporate finance and the M&A transactions landscape, with a focus on Transaction Diligence, Valuation, Modeling & Economics and mid-size M&A Advisory. By joining us, you will be stepping into an environment marked by ambition, drive to perform, resilience and our all comprising purpose of building a better working world. Our team is made up of dynamic and diverse individuals who thrive on collaboration, innovation, and entrepreneurial spirit, fueled by a categoric “YES, can do” mentality!
Based in our Zurich office, you will join one of the leading mid-market M&A teams in Switzerland, Europe, and globally, you will have the opportunity to work on high-profile sell- and buy-side M&A transactions with corporate clients, entrepreneurs, and financial sponsors. During this exceptional opportunity, you will gain hands on experience on various projects with a steep learning curve. This internship may also provide an opportunity to join the team in a full-time capacity.
Your Key Responsibilities
Preparation of transaction documents such as information memorandum, teaser, management presentation;
Company valuations using market and comparable transaction multiples and the DCF method;
Assist in the execution of M&A transactions from pitch to close;
In-depth industry and company analyses;
Preparation of potential buyer and target lists;
Support in the due diligence process;
Sharpen your technical skills in areas such as accounting, business valuations and financial modeling;
Support on multiple projects simultaneously, ensuring that tight deadlines are met.
What We Look For
Completed Bachelor’s degree or advanced stage of Master’s degree with excellent academic track record in business administration, finance, economics, etc;
First experience in relevant fields, ideally in M&A (M&A boutique, investment banking, Big Four) or in private equity, investment management, transaction diligence, etc;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and German. Additional fluency in French advantageous;
Proficiency in Office applications (Excel, PowerPoint, etc);
Exceptional analytical abilities and strong organizational skills;
Strong decision-making skills with the ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment;
Collaborative team player with a proactive mindse
